# The daily backup's timer (SPEC-064 R4, R6; ADR-064): once a day at 03:24, a minute of the hour that
# no job of the table, no reserved slot and no minute of the predecessor's schedule holds. A run missed
# while the host was down is made up at the next start, and a short random delay keeps it out of step
# with the other timers. The calendar is written in UTC; the private rail renders it in the owner's
# zone. With no Unit=, the timer starts the service of its own name.
[Unit]
Description=DeckStreak's daily backup, once a day

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* 03:24:00 UTC
Persistent=true
RandomizedDelaySec=30s
AccuracySec=1us

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
